    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 4th centers on a high-ceiling core anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 83.29 efficiency score. Facing Bello, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a favorable 4.43 xERA matchup and a significant +14% platoon edge, further bolstered by an impressive 25-PA BvP history against the right-hander. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier are **Kyle Tucker** (74.31) and **Andy Pages** (68.57); both are set to exploit a mediocre Ryne Nelson, with **Andy Pages** climbing into the 68+ range due to his projected slotting in the #2 hole. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.75) carries a marginal score, his projection is hampered by a stern matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA arm in Sale, though he remains a high-floor pivot given his placement in the #3 spot.\n\nDown the order, **Brayan Rocchio** (52.14) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.86) provide sufficient depth, though they face stiff resistance from Rod\u00f3n and Wheeler, respectively. **Jackson Merrill** is navigating a particularly difficult environment, facing an elite catcher and an SP known for suppressing stolen bases, which directly impacts our primary scarcity target. **Coby Mayo** (50.44) rounds out the active lineup, holding just above our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor despite a slight negative platoon adjustment against Bello.\n\nThe most notable bench decision today involved **Miguel Andujar**, whose 35.83 score fell well below our threshold. While **Miguel Andujar** benefits from the same park and SP context as **Jackson Merrill**, his heavy negative platoon split against right-handed pitching necessitated his removal from the active roster. As we look ahead, we continue to monitor the IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, whose absence leaves a significant production void in our quest for category dominance. We are currently proceeding with extreme caution regarding the lineup stability of **Kyle Tucker** 